<ui version="4.0">
 <class>SLIAFlow</class>
 <widget class="qMRMLWidget" name="SLIAFlow">
  <property name="geometry">
   <rect>
    <x>0</x>
    <y>0</y>
    <width>440</width>
    <height>520</height>
   </rect>
  </property>
  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout">
   <item>
    <widget class="QLabel" name="prototypeWarningLabel">
     <property name="text">
      <string>&lt;b&gt;Prototype only - not clinically validated.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Do not use with private or identifiable patient data.</string>
     </property>
     <property name="wordWrap">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QGroupBox" name="operatorGroupBox">
     <property name="title">
      <string>Operator</string>
     </property>
     <layout class="QFormLayout" name="operatorFormLayout">
      <item row="0" column="0">
       <widget class="QLabel" name="liveSourceLabel">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Live source:</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="0" column="1">
       <widget class="QComboBox" name="liveSourceSelector">
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>What the LiveView panel shows. Laptop camera: this laptop's camera, standing in for the acquisition system's live view. LiveView from the app: the colour camera frames IUMA's acquisition app sends on its LiveView port; connect under Connections first. Changing the source stops the one that runs.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="SlicerParameterName" stdset="0">
         <string>liveSource</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="1" column="0">
       <widget class="QLabel" name="captureActionsLabel">
        <property name="text">
         <string>LiveView:</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="1" column="1">
       <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="captureActionsLayout">
        <item>
         <widget class="QPushButton" name="startButton">
          <property name="enabled">
           <bool>false</bool>
          </property>
          <property name="toolTip">
           <string>Show the chosen live source in the LiveView panel: this laptop's camera, or LiveView from IUMA's acquisition app.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Start</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <widget class="QPushButton" name="stopButton">
          <property name="enabled">
           <bool>false</bool>
          </property>
          <property name="toolTip">
           <string>Stop the live source. The laptop camera is released for other applications.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Stop</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </item>
      <item row="2" column="0">
       <widget class="QLabel" name="captureLabel">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Capture:</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="2" column="1">
       <widget class="QPushButton" name="captureButton">
        <property name="enabled">
         <bool>false</bool>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Freeze LiveView, save the frame, run UC1 and the blood-vessel enhancement (UC2) in the background on the cube chosen under Cube source, and show the cube in HS Cube. Available while a live source shows a current frame and no capture is in progress.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="text">
         <string>Capture</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="3" column="0">
       <widget class="QLabel" name="resultOutputLabel">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Delineation output:</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="3" column="1">
       <widget class="QComboBox" name="resultOutputSelector">
        <property name="enabled">
         <bool>false</bool>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Select what the Tumour Delineation panel shows. Each UC1 output is shown on its own, as UC1 wrote it. svm.bmp and knn.bmp paint each pixel with its class: green normal tissue, red tumour, blue hypervascularised, black background. kmeans.bmp colours clusters with no fixed meaning, and pca.bmp is not a classification.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="SlicerParameterName" stdset="0">
         <string>resultOutput</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="4" column="0">
       <widget class="QLabel" name="cubeDisplayLabel">
        <property name="text">
         <string>HS Cube shows:</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="4" column="1">
       <widget class="QComboBox" name="cubeDisplaySelector">
        <property name="enabled">
         <bool>false</bool>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Bands: the calibrated cube one band at a time, with the band's wavelength on the panel; scroll the panel to change band. Colour preview: the bands nearest 650, 550 and 470 nm shown as red, green and blue, reflectance 0 to 1.0 on one fixed scale. It is a band composite, not a photograph. Click a pixel of HS Cube in either view to plot its spectrum under Pixel spectrum.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="5" column="0">
       <widget class="QLabel" name="cubeSourceLabel">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Cube source:</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="5" column="1">
       <widget class="QComboBox" name="cubeSourceSelector">
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Cube on disk: Capture reads the calibrated cube of the capture chosen under Recorded capture (simulated acquisition). Last cube from the app: HS Cube shows the last complete cube received from IUMA's acquisition app under Connections, and Capture runs UC1 and the blood-vessel enhancement on it. A raw uint16 cube is shown but not classified.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="SlicerParameterName" stdset="0">
         <string>cubeSource</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="6" column="0">
       <widget class="QLabel" name="captureListLabel">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Recorded capture:</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item row="6" column="1">
       <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="captureListLayout">
        <item>
         <widget class="QComboBox" name="captureSelector">
          <property name="sizePolicy">
           <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
            <horstretch>1</horstretch>
            <verstretch>0</verstretch>
           </sizepolicy>
          </property>
          <property name="toolTip">
           <string>The IUMA capture under input/ that Capture reads while Cube source is Cube on disk. Every session starts on S-N-002-04. A capture that is no longer in input/ is marked (not found). The list is read when SLIAFlow is entered and when Refresh is pressed. docs/development/capture_compatibility.md says which captures run through UC1 and UC2.</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <widget class="QPushButton" name="captureRefreshButton">
          <property name="toolTip">
           <string>Read the captures in input/ again, for one added or removed while Slicer runs.</string>
          </property>
          <property name="text">
           <string>Refresh</string>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
